<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarekat Islam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarekat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was an Indonesian organisation founded in 1912 out of an association of Muslim batik traders, and under Oemar Said Tjokroaminoto it became the first mass political movement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, with hundreds of thousands of members by 1919. It called for self-government and the economic advancement of Indonesians. In the early 1920s it split between its Islamic leadership and a communist wing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarekat-islam.jpg" alt="Sarekat Islam" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Respublika Narodnaya · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LogoSI.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
